# What `docker build` does not send to the builder. The build context is the whole
# repository, so without this file it would ship .venv (about 2 GB of the host's
# own environment, built for the host) and .env (the keys) to every build.
#
# Both Dockerfiles copy only what they name, so nothing below could reach an image
# anyway. This file keeps it out of the build context too, which keeps builds fast
# and keeps the keys out of the builder.

.env
.venv/
.git/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Data is not code. The corpus is mounted by compose, uploads and model weights
# live on volumes, and runs are this machine's history.
data/
